  {
   "type": "text",
   "role": "user",
   "content": "Compare OCPP 1.6J and 2.0.1 briefly.",
   "timestamp": 1790130000020,
   "toolCalls": "",
   "extra": [],
   "id": "e7f4b3ff-a2bd-4b9a-9c53-2b75fbbd9221",
   "convId": "48c869a1-61a0-4f52-9382-0628a5dc9f2a",
   "parent": "01f5bfb8-fb84-4642-82e4-55b759ce78f2",
   "children": [
    "386060ed-6ee4-4c2b-9ce2-1e7d382116cf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "role": "assistant",
   "content": "Sure. Here is a compact comparison of the two protocols:\n\n- **OCPP 1.6J** uses JSON over WebSocket and is what most chargers in the field speak today.\n- **OCPP 2.0.1** adds device management, better security profiles, and ISO 15118 support.\n\nMigration usually happens charger by charger, so a CSMS must speak both for years.",
